From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iOS Research Runtime <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] darwin: instantiate a minimal GPEX PCIe root bus

The darwin machine has no PCI bus, so generic PCI devices fail before guest
boot with "No PCI bus found for device nvme". Realize QEMU's generic GPEX
host bridge so -device nvme can attach to a PCIe root bus.

Use the QOM type name directly so this bounded probe does not depend on an
additional header-context hunk. This intentionally does not yet map ECAM/MMIO
or describe PCIe to the Apple DeviceTree.
---
 hw/arm/darwin.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/arm/darwin.c b/hw/arm/darwin.c
--- a/hw/arm/darwin.c
+++ b/hw/arm/darwin.c
@@ -224,6 +224,10 @@ static void darwin_init(MachineState *ms) {
     dt_root = info->dtree_f.buf;
 
     check_dtree(dt_root);
+
+    DeviceState *pcie = qdev_new("gpex-host");
+    qdev_prop_set_uint32(pcie, "num-irqs", 0);
+    sysbus_realize_and_unref(SYS_BUS_DEVICE(pcie), &error_fatal);
 
     info->has_mte = kc_uses_mte(info->bootkc_f.buf);
 
-- 
